---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website Terms"
  description="Terms for using The OC Events Market website."
  noindex
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Website Terms</h1>
    <p>
      These terms cover general website use only and remain subject to legal review. They are not a
      contract for event planning and do not replace a signed proposal or service agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Website information</h2>
    <p>
      Website copy is provided for general information. Service availability, responsibilities,
      inclusions, staffing, hours on the event day, pricing, and vendor terms are controlled by the
      approved proposal and signed agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>No booking through a text</h2>
    <p>
      A text conversation does not reserve a date, create a client relationship, guarantee
      availability, or confirm a service. A vendor introduction does not create a partnership or
      recommendation.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside services</h2>
    <p>
      Vendors, venues, and linked services may have separate contracts, policies, pricing, licenses,
      and responsibilities. Those terms should be reviewed directly with the relevant provider.
    </p>

    <h2>Photography and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses a mix of licensed editorial photography and event media supplied to the studio.
      An event image does not by itself establish the planner’s scope, a vendor partnership, or an
      included service. Publication rights, credits, and permissions remain the responsibility of
      the applicable rights holder.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing terms and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about the service agreement belong in the booking process. Website copy is not a
      substitute for the governing terms in a signed agreement.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
